    "### TASK 1.2. OBSERVATIONS\n",
    "\n",
    "In a markdown cell, answer the following:\n",
    "\n",
    "(1). What test accuracy did your vanilla RNN achieve?\n",
    "\n",
    "(2). Plot training loss vs. epoch. Does the model converge? Any sign of overfitting?\n",
    "\n",
    "(3). What is the vanishing gradient problem and why might it affect this model on long reviews? (2–3 sentences, no equations needed.)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 16,
   "id": "770521d3",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/markdown": [
       "(1) The final test accuracy was 62.26%."
      ],
      "text/plain": [
       "<IPython.core.display.Markdown object>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "text/markdown": [
       "(2) Yes the model shows signs of converging. After 5 epochs the train loss and test loss are both decreasing. Signs of overfitting may be present as test_loss and train_loss diverge. More epochs would be required to confirm."
      ],
      "text/plain": [
       "<IPython.core.display.Markdown object>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "text/markdown": [
       "(3) During training backpropagation is used to determine the rate at which the loss value changes with each weight in the network. For every nurmerical operation taken by the network, backpropagation will compute the partial gradient of the operation and multiply that with the backpropagated gradient. For long input sequences, the RNN has to recurse over the sequence and if partial gradient terms are less than 1 (or larger than 1) in magnitude, values shrink towards $0$ (or $\\infty$ (exploding gradients)). Ultimately this means early timesteps get almost no learning signal and the RNN will fail to learn long-range dependencies.\n"
      ],
      "text/plain": [
       "<IPython.core.display.Markdown object>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "application/vnd.plotly.v1+json": {
       "config": {
        "plotlyServerURL": "https://plot.ly"
       },
       "data": [
        {
         "hovertemplate": "variable=train_loss<br>Epoch=%{x}<br>Loss=%{y}<extra></extra>",
