      "text/markdown": [
       "### TASK 4.1. HEAD-TO-HEAD SUMMARY TABLE\n",
       "\n",
       "Fill in the following table in your notebook. All values should come from your actual runs.\n",
       "\n",
       "| Model| TestAccuracy | Parameters | Avg Epoch Time |\n",
       "| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n",
       "| Vanilla RNN | 0.64 | 2659586 | 3.01 |\n",
       "| LSTM | 0.87 | 3482370 | 23.44 |\n",
       "| BRNN | 0.88 | 4928770 | 42.39 |\n",
       "\n",
       "Write 3–4 sentences interpreting the trade-off between accuracy, model size, and training speed across the three architectures.\n",
       "\n",
       "Model accuracy increases with parameter count and training time. The Vanilla RNN has the lowest test accuracy at 64% with ~2.7 million parameters and an average epoch time of 3.1 seconds. The LSTM and BRNN have similarly high test accuracy of 87% and 88% respectively, however the LSTM contains only ~3.5 million parameters compared to ~4.9 million of the BRNN and has a significantly shorter training time at ~23 seconds/epoch compared to 42 seconds/epoch. While the performance of the LSTM and BRNN appear similar, the train history for the BRNN demonstrates faster and more stable convergence compared to the LSTM.\n"
      ],
      "text/plain": [
       "<IPython.core.display.Markdown object>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
